RF.put("questb:b19",{"8579":{"id":8579,"t":"Mortal Champions","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Qiraji Lord's Insignia The Prophet Skeram in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Emperor Vek'nilash in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"We sense the presence of our enslaved brethren deeper inside Ahn'Qiraj; yet not even an army of dragons would be enough to rescue them, ‹race›.\nThe same spell that imprisoned them would place us firmly under C'Thun's control should we come any closer to him.\nThe Old God has foreseen our arrival. All hope is lost. What difference could a mere mortal like you possibly make?","done":"I see that you're no ordinary mortal, ‹name›. Your chances against the Old God, however infinitely small, are greater than ours at this point. After all, while he expects dragons at his doorstep, he is not prepared for someone like you.\nJust as Anachronos and Staghelm defeated the Qiraji a thousand years ago through the alliance of mortal and dragon races, we too shall form a pact. Gain the trust of the Bronze Dragonflight and you'll gain our trust. Only then we shall make a true champion out of you.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Quest ID 8579\nThe chain\n47 quests at level 60, 16,500 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions this quest\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] One quest for each class\nWarrior , Warrior , Warrior , Warrior , Warrior , Priest , Priest , Priest , Priest , Shaman , Priest , Shaman , Shaman , Shaman , Shaman , Mage , Hunter , Paladin , Paladin , Paladin , Paladin , Mage , Mage , Mage , Mage , Rogue , Rogue , Rogue , Rogue , Rogue , Paladin , Hunter , Hunter , Hunter , Hunter , Warlock , Warlock , Warlock , Warlock , Warlock , Druid , Druid , Druid , Druid , Druid\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n[ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n3,300 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8659":{"id":8659,"t":"Striker's Pauldrons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of War, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of War Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nStriker's Pauldrons\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8659\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Striker's Pauldrons this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of War, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8499":{"id":8499,"t":"The Alliance Needs Thorium Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 48.","obj":"Bring 20 Thorium Bars to Dame Twinbraid at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Thorium Bar","desc":"It is very kind of you to inquire about the needs that the Alliance has. In addition to all of the other collection efforts underway, we are in need of a great quantity of thorium bars, which is the task that I am in charge of. The thorium will be used in the creation of many different things for the war, foremost of which is the construction of a battalion of steam tanks to be airlifted into Silithus as soon as they are completed. Can you aid us in this endeavor, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Oh, a shipment from my brother? Splendid! Fortune truly shines on me today!","done":"So Gnoarn doesn't trust my reconnaissance abilities? I wonder why...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":32.1,"n":"Dame Twinbraid","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"97539":{"id":97539,"t":"Silky sutures","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return 12 Surgical Spidersilk to Doctor Gregory Victor in Hammerfall, Arathi Highlands.\n12 Surgical Spidersilk","desc":"This encampment is being left to rot. The siege damage stands, unrepaired, as if neglect were policy. I won't permit that same decay here. The infirmary answers to me, and I intend to keep it functional.\nWe are nearly out of supplies. I'm going to need more equipment--enough to keep the workers and guards on their feet.\nUnder pressure, we can make quite an effective field suture using twisted spider silk.\n‹class›, bring me some from the spiders that stalk these highlands.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.4,"y":36.8,"n":"Doctor Gregory Victor","s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"739":{"id":739,"t":"Murdaloc","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Agmond's killer, Murdaloc.\nSlay 12 Stonevault Bonesnappers.\nReport to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.\nMurdaloc slain\nStonevault Bonesnapper slain : 0/ 12","desc":"Agmond's tracks lead from the west. It is easy to tell from the bloody smears across rock and sand that the dwarf crawled some distance.\nAnd here he died.\nUpon close inspection, the word \"Murdaloc\" is roughly scrawled in a patch of Badlands sandstone.\nScrawled next to Agmond's dead hand.","rew":"You will receive:\nRock Pulverizer\nExperience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have news of Agmond's fate? Did you find him?","done":"This is sobering news, ‹name›. But Agmond had a strong arm and a fierce hammer-swing, and his skull was as thick as they come! Although he was killed by those cursed troggs I'm sure he took a lot of them down with him.\nBadlands Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":50.9,"y":62.4,"n":"Battered Dwarven Skeleton","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.9,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97939":{"id":97939,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Elisa Steelhand in Auberdine in Darkshore to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96659":{"id":96659,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Supply Bundle to Kaga Wildhoof near Bloodhoof Village.\nProvided: Supply Bundle","desc":"Wait, ‹name›. I have another ask of you, before you leave us.\nThere is an adventurer by the name of Kaga Wildhoof who has made camp just outside of Bloodhoof Village. She has greatly helped me in the past, and now I see my chance to repay her. Could you deliver these supplies to her?","back":"Are you here to learn about camping in the wilderness?","done":"Chief Hawkwind sent you? I told him back then I needed no compensation, but it seems he hasn't listened. Thank you, ‹class›.\nHey, you've got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.2,"y":76,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94339":{"id":94339,"t":"Craftsmans writ field repair bot 74a","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Field Repair Bot 74A\nField Repair Bot 74A","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Field Repair Bot 74A, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Field Repair Bot 74A Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94339","cats":["crafting"]},"94259":{"id":94259,"t":"Craftsmans writ nature protection potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Nature Protection Potion\nNature Protection Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Nature Protection Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+125 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+125 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Have you come to aid the Emerald Circle?","done":"We are in dire need of more of these potions here in Felwood. Though there are many corruptive forces at play here, nature itself is known to lash out violently when provoked.\nI suspect this will not be the last time you replenish our supply, ‹name›. Thank you kindly for your assistance.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.1,"y":82.2,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7939":{"id":7939,"t":"More Dense Grinding Stones","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"8 Dense Grinding Stone","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket","back":"‹name›, thank you for all the help you've given me. I really can't thank you enough!\nAlthough my need is no longer great... if you bring me more dense grinding stones, I still have more Darkmoon Faire tickets for you.","done":"Thanks much, ‹name›. Here's your Darkmoon Faire tickets!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.6,"y":46.4,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.5,"y":69.9,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"98899":{"id":98899,"t":"Darkspear islands clash","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.\nIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+150 reputation with Theramore Expeditionary Force\nLevel 59 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 55 57 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 98899","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1459":{"id":1459,"t":"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 7 vials of Scorpashi Venom and 3 Aged Kodo Hides to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\n7 Scorpashi Venom Scorpashi Snapper 50 % , Scorpashi Lasher 50 % , Scorpashi Venomlash 50 %\n3 Aged Kodo Hide Aged Kodo","desc":"Next on Leftwitch's list is... let's see... hmm. Oh, here it is.\nSimple enough, but pretty explicit in his directions. He needs venom from the scorpashi, and hide from some kodo. The fine print says both are from specific creatures: the venom's got to come from any of the scorpashi, and the hide's got to come from an aged kodo, not the dying or ancient ones.\nMages, I tell ya, some of the stuff they want... it's just weird.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Sorry I couldn't tell you where to find the kodo or the scorpashi. I'm not terribly familiar with the area, and I haven't had time to explore.","done":"Your help here's a boon, ‹name›. You're cutting my time spent here in Desolace by half at least. I'll be back in Ironforge warming my feet in no time with your help.\nWhen we get this list taken care of, and I'm back home, look me up, I'll buy you an ale for sure.\nBut until then, let's get the rest of these reagents gathered.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"98739":{"id":98739,"t":"Blessings of the great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Dendrite.","desc":"Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.\nMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one.","done":"<Dendrite makes another invisible gesture in the air above him as you approach. Another aura of power comes over him, and he smiles ever so slightly.>\nI sense the cunning and ferocity of the cat within you that was not present when I sent you to meet the Great Cat Spirit. In your eyes I can sense you now understand the stealth and speed needed to adopt this nature.\nNow you may learn to focus your cunning and adopt the true nature of the cat and call upon its spirit.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":54.6,"y":75,"n":"Great Cat Spirit","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"179":{"id":179,"t":"Dwarven Outfitters","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sten Stoutarm would like 8 pieces of Tough Wolf Meat.\n8 Tough Wolf Meat Ragged Young Wolf 80 % , Ragged Timber Wolf 80 % , Young Wolf 80 % , Timber Wolf 80 %","desc":"What do we have here? You look as though you might need something to keep your hands warm, hm?\nI'll tell you what would help: a pair of nice, warm gloves. And, being the kind soul that I am, I'd be more than happy to provide you with a suitable pair. I've one condition, however.\nI need you to go get me some wolf meat. Nice arrangement, hm? You bring me some wolf meat, and I'll make sure you don't lose any digits to frostbite. Well, what do you say?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRabbit Handler Gloves Wolf Handler Gloves Boar Handler Gloves\nExperience: 80\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Wolves giving you a bit of trouble? You'd do well to avoid the fangs and claws and other sharp bits, yes?","done":"Ah! Wonderful. The wolf meat should do nicely. Oh, don't worry, ‹name›, I wouldn't forget my part of the bargain. Here, one of these should fit you.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"419":{"id":419,"t":"The Lost Pilot","lv":10,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Pilot Hildelve.","desc":"My friend and fellow Siege Engine pilot, Mori Hildelve, is lost in the hills. We were looking for a rare ore that's needed for a high-grade blastpowder, and during our search he drove his engine up a steep hill and busted it!\nStill convinced that ore was in these mountains, Hildelve charged me to guard our engines while he continued on foot, searching.\nIt's been days, and I've heard some beastly growls in the hills at night. Mori's tough as nails, but I'm worried.\nPlease, ‹name›. Find him.","rew":"You will receive:\nSiege Brigade Vest\nExperience: 420\n+50 reputation with Ironforge\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Here is the corpse of a dwarf -- mauled, frozen, and picked clean by mountain scavengers. Clutched in its hand is a book containing the roughly scribbled notes of Mori Hildelve. And around its frame, still in superior condition, is a Brigadier's Vest.\nThis grisly scene must have been where the Siege Engine pilot met his end.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":83.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Pilot Hammerfoot","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":79.7,"y":36.2,"n":"A Dwarven Corpse","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"1219":{"id":1219,"t":"The Orc Report","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Spy's Report to a Theramore Lieutenant.\nSpy's Report\nProvided: Spy's Report","desc":"Sifting through the loose dirt, the severed hand of an orc is found. And clutched in the hand is a bone-carved tube. And in the tube is a dirt-stained parchment.\nThe parchment is written in orcish... and it looks important.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have a report to make?","done":"Hm... I can't read orcish very well, but this looks like a report... written by an orc spy!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":55.4,"y":25.9,"n":"Loose Dirt","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":65.1,"y":47.2,"n":"Theramore Lieutenant","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"2979":{"id":2979,"t":"Dark Ceremony","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rok Orhan in Camp Mojache wants you to find a Gordunni Orb.\nGordunni Orb Gordunni Mage-Lord","desc":"These seem to be plans for some sort of dark ceremony, ‹name›. From what I can make out, this ritual is conducted by the Gordunni mage-lords.\nFind one of these mage-lords, and from him, gather an orb.\nThe orb of a mage contains great power, and will help us discover more about this ceremony and the magic that the Gordunni wield.","rew":"Experience: 4,050\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"We must discover more about why the Gordunni are here, ‹name›.","done":"This orb will provide us with more information about the Gordunni... which we will then use in planning their downfall, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Rok Orhan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"499":{"id":499,"t":"Elixir of Suffering","lv":22,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Umpi the Elixir of Suffering.\nElixir of Suffering\nProvided: Elixir of Suffering","desc":"It will take but a moment for me to mix these components into what I have deemed an Elixir of Suffering.\nThere we go! Ah, nothing brightens a gloomy day in these miserable foothills like bringing a little suffering into the world.\nLet us see if our little potion has achieved its desired effect.\nGive my assistant Umpi a taste of what the Dark Lady has planned for both humans and Scourge alike.","rew":"Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Ribbit!","done":"Croak!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.5,"y":19.1,"n":"Umpi","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"659":{"id":659,"t":"Hints of a New Plague?","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Quae and Kinelory near the Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands.","desc":"Hail, and well met, ‹name›. I lead a group of adventurers investigating odd happenings in this area.\nMy cousin in Hillsbrad recently put down his dog Stanley because the animal mystically grew to an immense size and savagely attacked anyone who came near him.\nI believe the undead are involved, and we're looking for signs to prove as much.\nTwo of my companions, Quae and Kinelory, headed to the Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands, and haven't checked in for days. Find them for me? I grow concerned.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Try and stay as quiet as possible, traveler.\nOrcs don't take too well to being spied on, and there is more to this farm than meets the eye.\nHillsbrad Foothills Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.3,"y":59,"n":"Phin Odelic","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.8,"n":"Quae","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"94979":{"id":94979,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands.\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.\nTame an Ornery Galestrider\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"You've proven you can tame the river's crawler, now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the Galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.\nTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.\nShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.","back":"You will learn, Naanariel, and one day you will be a great ‹class›.","done":"You're back already! Impressive speed, Naanariel!","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Quel'ana Quickgale","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9299":{"id":9299,"t":"Note from the Front","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 45 instead of 55.","obj":"Take the Careworn Note to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Careworn Note\nProvided: A Careworn Note","desc":"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","back":"Yes? What do you have there?","done":"How tragic. These words, clearly meant for someone the soldier loved, never made it to their destination. The events detailed happened years ago; I'm not sure if the intended recipient still lives.\nThere is hope yet, however. With the names and information he gives, I might be able to locate the family! It will take some research, but the librarian in Stormwind owes me a favor...\nThank you for bringing this to me. With your help, we may be able to grant someone peace of mind at least.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"1939":{"id":1939,"t":"High Sorcerer Andromath","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with High Sorcerer Andromath.","desc":"High Sorcerer Andromath wishes to speak with you, ‹name›. He is at the top of the wizard's sanctum, in the mage's district of Stormwind.\nIt would be wise to speak with him, for Andromath is one of the most powerful mages not locked away in Dalaran. Council with him is high council indeed.","rew":"Experience: 1,050","done":"Greetings, ‹name›. I am pleased to see you, and hope you have time to listen to an old man's words...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.7,"y":87.6,"n":"High Sorcerer Andromath","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"96259":{"id":96259,"t":"Defending the dead","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 10 Gloomrise Hatchlings and 5 Gloomrise Soldiers.\nGloomrise Hatchling slain : 0/ 10\nGloomrise Soldier slain : 0/ 5","desc":"There is an ancient tauren burial ground at the place called Gloomrise, just northwest of this camp. Of late it has been infested with a particularly vicious brood of spiders. These spiders not only pose a threat to the people of Mulgore, they are also damaging a site that most tauren consider to be sacred.\nIt would be of great service if you could travel to Gloomrise and put an end to this infestation. The ancestors will surely smile upon you if you see this done.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+150 reputation with Earthen Ring\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Muln Earthfury","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9059":{"id":9059,"t":"Cryptstalker Handguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Cryptstalker Handguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Handguards, 8 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Handguards\n8 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Handguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Handguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1779":{"id":1779,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Symbol of Life and speak to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge.\nProvided: Symbol of Life","desc":"I want you to take this, ‹name›. It is called the Symbol of Life.\nYou've proven charitable and patient, and now I want you to prove just how adept you've become in both combat, and power.\nMy husband Muiredon returned recently from an encounter with some Dark Iron dwarves, and he barely escaped with his life--he's over there having his wounds healed by one of our priests.\nTake the Symbol and speak to him. If you can help him, then we will speak again soon. May the Light shine upon you.","done":"*cough*\nGood day to ya, ‹class›. Don't mind me wounds, the good priest 'ere'll take care of ol' Muiredon in time. Not needin' the power of that Symbol of Life ya got there quite yet.\nSo, me wife sent ya o'er to speak to me, huh? Fair 'nough. I'll take the time to talk to ya-I'll tell ya exactly wut happened to Muiredon and his best friend Narm, a ‹class› jus' like yerself.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.9,"y":22.4,"n":"Muiredon Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"91859":{"id":91859,"t":"A curious pair","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Deathguard Baldren about the mysterious Earthen Ring travelers who recently passed through The Sepulcher.","desc":"Cutting straight to it, these \"dignitaries\" are no ordinary diplomats. One was a Tauren. Ordinary enough for the Earthen Ring, but the other--and you'll scarcely believe this--was an elf. A *high* elf. They were cloaked, but I've seen quel'dorei before and I'd bet my good pinky finger that's what I saw.\nWhy was an elf accompanying a Tauren through horde territory? Well, your guess is as good as mine. That's as much as I know, so I'd suggest speaking with Deathguard Baldren near the entrance to town.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"I might not care for you paladins, but I will say that your timing is impeccable. It's better to be lucky than good, I suppose?","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41,"n":"Trevan Rol","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":45.6,"y":41.8,"n":"Deathguard Baldren","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94819":{"id":94819,"t":"Contingency plan","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"‹name›, your High Priestess Mims would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my clever friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Mims should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. She will be waiting.\nStormwind City Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":24.8,"y":10,"n":"High Priestess Mims","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"19":{"id":19,"t":"Tharil'zun","lv":25,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Tharil'zun's Head to Marshal Marris in Redridge.\nTharil'zun's Head Tharil'zun","desc":"Blackrock Outrunners and Renegades are running ambushes between here and Stonewatch Keep. The leader of the Outrunners is an orc named Tharil'zun--we want this orc. Bring me the head of Tharil'zun!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFire Hardened Buckler Orc Crusher\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Orc pressure from Blackrock is still tense. But have you at least rid us of Tharil'zun?","done":"Tharil'zun was a vicious, crafty orc. Well done - I'm sure he didn't go down easy. Here is your reward, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":28.4,"y":49,"n":"Marshal Marris","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8819":{"id":8819,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Stormwind. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.9,"y":32.2,"n":"Darnassus Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.4,"y":74.5,"n":"Officer Maloof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"1859":{"id":1859,"t":"Therzok","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Lower your voice, ‹name›. Yeah, I know your name. Was told to keep an eye out for an orc by your description.\nFrom what we've heard about you, you can handle yourself in combat, and aren't opposed to a little sneakery from time to time.\nAm I right?\nAnyways, you should go see Therzok in Orgrimmar. He's got an offer for you to hear.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"Very good, I'm glad Kaplak was able to get a hold of you.\nWe have some things to speak of, not the least of which is your future with the Hand.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":43.7,"n":"Kaplak","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.7,"y":53.6,"n":"Therzok","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2259":{"id":2259,"t":"Erion Shadewhisper","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Contact Erion Shadewhisper in Darnassus.","desc":"Do not worry, ‹name›, I am not sending you to see Syurna. Erion requires your presence at the Cenarion Enclave. Make haste!","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"It is time to branch out, ‹race› - the world awaits.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.4,"y":60.1,"n":"Jannok Breezesong","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.5,"y":25.9,"n":"Erion Shadewhisper","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8899":{"id":8899,"t":"Dearest Colara,","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Immaculate Letter to Colara Dean outside the bank in Stormwind.\nImmaculate Letter\nProvided: Immaculate Letter","desc":"How to describe her beauty? Thousands of years of words and I am at a loss.\nThese mortals confound the mind and leave us babbling fools.\nI've stared at these words too long. No more eloquent meaning can I squeeze from them. No, she must have it now, or some other suitor will surely steal her eye.","back":"Hello there, handsome. Something I can help you with?","done":"I've never received something like this before. How lovely!\nDarnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":42,"y":42.3,"n":"Aldris Fourclouds","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.7,"y":75.5,"n":"Colara Dean","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8979":{"id":8979,"t":"Fenstad's Hunch","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Cologne Bottle and 1 Perfume Bottle to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity's Apothecarium.\nCologne Bottle sold by Innkeeper Allison , sold by Innkeeper Firebrew , sold by Innkeeper Saelienne , sold by Innkeeper Gryshka and 4 more\nPerfume Bottle sold by Innkeeper Allison , sold by Innkeeper Firebrew , sold by Innkeeper Saelienne , sold by Innkeeper Gryshka and 4 more","desc":"I believe I know the cause of this recent behavior. Have you smelled the new fragrance on the wind, over the stink of the canals? The new colognes and perfumes that have come into fashion?\nOur thinking has been clouded by some foul alchemy.\nThere is only one way to be sure - bring a bottle of cologne and perfume to my friend, Apothecary Zinge. The Royal Apothecary Society will find the truth.\nI will reimburse you for their purchase when you return.","back":"How may I serve you?","done":"Another one of Fenstad's obsessions, I see. Does he think that the Royal Apothecary Society has nothing better to do than to perform his little investigations?\nVery well, I will humor him once again.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":66.7,"y":44.7,"n":"Fenstad Argyle","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94499":{"id":94499,"t":"Call of water","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at Stonewatch Falls near the Nightcrawler Murlocs and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.\nFull Red Waterskin","desc":"Aye, Redridge drinks deep from Lake Everstill, but by the time the waters tumble down Stonewatch Falls, somethin' has seeped in. The murlocs down there are big, twisted brutes. Not like the ones ye find here or in the Loch. Lucky for the townsfolk they keep to the base o' the falls.\nBring a sampling to me. I've a mind to find out if it's magic, venom, or somethin' worse that's taintin' the waters near that old fort.","back":"The folk o' Lakeshire don't ken how good they've got it -- fresh water flowin' right at their boots, keepin' their nets full, their crops green, and their coin purses jinglin'. Even when the kingdom's guard can barely spare a lad with a sword, they've got Everstill watchin' over 'em.","done":"Aye, this is good water, Theinn. The magic used by the shadowseers in the region must be changin' the murlocs. Nothin' but pure water, this be. Yer dedication to the task at hand and abilities to seek out that which is needed proves you're ready for the next stage of your journey.\nOne more sample is all I need to create the reagent needed for your sapta. Norric will be pleased as well.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":65.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Hervdana Saegrund","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8259":{"id":8259,"t":"A more fitting reward","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nSkyfury Helm","done":"Ah, ‹name›... your effort against Darkreaver was extraordinary - an effort, may I add, that deserved a much better reward than you received. Please, accept this helm as an additional gift to you for your accomplishments in Scholomance.\nAgain, thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.6,"y":36.2,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8739":{"id":8739,"t":"Hive'Ashi Scout Report","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Contact Cenarion Scout Jalia inside Hive'Ashi and return the Hive'Ashi Scout Report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.\nHive'Ashi Scout Report\nTactical Task Briefing VIII\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing VIII","desc":"We've sent our best scouts deep into the silithid hives to gather intelligence. Scout Jalia has been watching the silithid movements at Hive'Ashi for several days now. Find her and obtain a written report. We need to be able to act on that information as soon as possible, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You'll find Scout Jalia inside Hive'Ashi. Hurry, ‹name›! Time is of the essence.","done":"Your efforts are greatly appreciated, ‹name›. I'll read these scouting reports right away, feel free to go over your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"99":{"id":99,"t":"Arugal's Folly","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Pyrewood Shackles to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\n6 Pyrewood Shackle Moonrage Leatherworker 80 % , Pyrewood Leatherworker 80 % , Moonrage Tailor 80 % , Pyrewood Tailor 80 % and 4 more","desc":"As my understanding of Arugal's magic grows so does my disdain for the hapless fool. I am close to completing my research on his so called remedy.\nMy knowledge will be complete when I learn what enchantment is causing the strange behavior going on in Pyrewood Village. By day, the peasants appear to be Human. But when the sun goes down the townsfolk turn into Moonrage Worgen.\nI need to draw energy from the enchanted shackles Arugal cast on them. Bring to me six enchanted Pyrewood Shackles, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLogsplitter Bonegrinding Pestle Cinder Wand\nExperience: 1,350\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you secured the Pyrewood Shackles yet, ‹name›?","done":"Your persistence is commendable. With the knowledge you helped me gather, Arugal will fall and his reckless magic shall be undone. Cheers to you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1059":{"id":1059,"t":"Reclaiming the Charred Vale","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Reclaimer's Robes.","obj":"Travel to Falfindel Waywarder on the border of Thousand Needles and Feralas.","desc":"The Bloodfuries have been subdued. But they will regroup soon enough if action is not taken.\nFar south of the Barrens lies a land known as Thousand Needles. If you travel west in Thousand Needles until you reach the lush forest's edge of Feralas, you will find a druid named Falfindel Waywarder.\nThis great and wise druid is capable of calling forth great forest spirits which can aid in the reclamation of the Charred Vale.\nSend word of our need! Seek him out at once!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTempered Bracers Constable Buckler Reclaimer's Robes\nNew in Forever: Reclaimer's Robes.\nExperience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Keeper Albagorm was wise to send you with such urgency.\nLet us see if we cannot call forth aid from the great forest to travel to the Charred Vale before it is too late.\nStonetalon Mountains Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":37.1,"y":8.1,"n":"Keeper Albagorm","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":89.6,"y":46.6,"n":"Falfindel Waywarder","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"579":{"id":579,"t":"Stormwind Library","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Library Scrip","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThe Story of Morgan Ladimore Legends of the Gurubashi, Volume 3","back":"King Anduin has placed great importance on learning, and thus has provided funds for making copies of various tomes and writings available to the public. It's very simple. You bring me a library scrip, and I can give you a copy of one of the available books.","done":"Do any of these titles interest you, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":75.1,"y":30.1,"n":"Donyal Tovald","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"339":{"id":339,"t":"Chapter I","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring pages 1, 4, 6, and 8 of Nesingwary's The Green Hills of Stranglethorn to Barnil Stonepot in order to complete Chapter I.\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 1 Roloch 2.7 % , Bookie Herod 2.4 % , Sergeant Malthus 1.9 % , Mosh'Ogg Butcher 1.6 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 4 Verifonix 1.6 % , Kurzen's Agent 1.5 % , Negolash 1.4 % , Saltscale Oracle 1.4 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 6 Verifonix 4.4 % , Roloch 2.7 % , Venture Co. Workboss 1.6 % , Kurzen Wrangler 1.5 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 8 Mosh'Ogg Butcher 8.3 % , Verifonix 1.6 % , Mogh the Undying 1.5 % , Captain Keelhaul 1.3 % and 4 more","desc":"Chapter I was quite riveting! Master Nesingwary sets the backdrop for the story and makes mention of his hunting companions, including me!\nBut that's besides the point. Let me see which pages are still missing. It seems pages 1, 4, 6 and 8 are still out there somewhere in the jungle!","rew":"You will receive:\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter I\nExperience: 775","back":"I don't suppose you were able to track down pages 1, 4, 6 and 8? Those four are all we need to piece Chapter I back together.","done":"At last! Chapter I is complete!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.5,"n":"Barnil Stonepot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3379":{"id":3379,"t":"Shadoweaver","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 40 instead of 46. Gives 4,700 experience instead of 6,750, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Kill the group of Shadow Silk Poachers that wander the Searing Gorge. Nilith has reason to believe that there are five of them that need to be exterminated. Return to Nilith in the Searing Gorge when this task is complete.\nShadowsilk Poacher slain : 0/ 5","desc":"The spiders of the Searing Gorge are an invaluable source of shadow silk. As you know, shadow silk is highly sought after by the artisans of our trade.\nRecently, a group of poachers has encroached upon these lands, carelessly slaying spiders en masse without so much as a thought as to the long term effect of their actions. The first task I ask of you, then, is a simple one: Find them... and end them.\nBegin your search to the north.\nIf you require assistance, speak with Raze.","rew":"You will receive:\nShadowy Bracers\nMoney: 1 45 1 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700","back":"What information do you have?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›.\nI am sure that this is a piece of shadoweave that you have not yet seen.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41,"y":74.9,"n":"Nilith Lokrav","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tailoring"]},"2499":{"id":2499,"t":"Oakenscowl","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 6s instead of 3s.","obj":"Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth wants you to collect the Gargantuan Tumor from Oakenscowl.\nGargantuan Tumor Oakenscowl","desc":"In a cave along the southern bank of the lake, a timberling named Oakenscowl is spreading corruption to all the creatures that make Lake Al'Ameth their home.\nI dared not get too close, but even from a distance, it is obvious: Oakenscowl is being poisoned by the largest tumor I have ever seen... I would call it gargantuan, even.\n‹name›, you have already done much to aid my efforts, but I ask of you one more task. Hunt down Oakenscowl and collect the tumor; remove this source of corruption from my home.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDirtwood Belt Moss-covered Gauntlets\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you located Oakenscowl yet, ‹race›?","done":"I knew you were more than capable of ridding the lake of that horrible beast.\nIt is a distressing situation; Oakenscowl was once a grand leader amongst his kind... but corruption does not discriminate between the lowly and the noble.\nThe size of this tumor is quite disturbing, but I must study it to learn more about the disease that upsets the timberling population.\nThank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"979":{"id":979,"t":"Find Ranshalla","lv":57,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Ranshalla in eastern Winterspring.","desc":"Yes, yes, these feathers seem to hold the same magical enchantment that I noticed previously... While I am not certain what we might find, I urge you to continue searching for answers, ‹name›.\nA colleague of mine recently traveled into Winterspring to observe the wildkin there, in their own habitat. Why don't you catch up with her and see what she has found?","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Hi! Erelas sent you? Great, I was just preparing to travel up to the caves now, and I wouldn't mind company.\nTeldrassil Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.5,"y":92,"n":"Erelas Ambersky","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":63.1,"y":59.5,"n":"Ranshalla","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"819":{"id":819,"t":"Chen's Empty Keg","lv":15,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find someone who knows about Chen's Empty Keg.\nChen's Empty Keg Chen's Empty Keg\nProvided: Chen's Empty Keg","desc":"A small placard on one of the ends of the keg says,\n\"Chen Stormstout-\nMay your spirit be raised and always raise your spirits.\"","rew":"Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yes?","done":"Well, I'll be...\nThis was one of Chen Stormstout's kegs. He traveled with Rexxar a long time ago. I haven't seen or heard about him in a kodo's age. I appreciate you bringing this to me, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":37.9,"y":16.2,"n":"Chen's Empty Keg","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":38.4,"n":"Brewmaster Drohn","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"899":{"id":899,"t":"Consumed by Hatred","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 60 Bristleback Quilboar Tusks to Mankrik at the Crossroads.\n60 Bristleback Quilboar Tusk Bristleback Geomancer 80 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 80 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 80 % , Bristleback Hunter 80 %","desc":"Perhaps you know the pain of uncertainty, perhaps not, ‹class›. But know this: I stand here every day, from the sun's rising till its decline, scouring the horizon for more of those monsters. I've killed every pig man I've come across since, but my thirst for their blood is far from quenched. Perhaps instead of heading north to the Crossroads I should have headed to Taurajo.\nYou, ‹class›--you could help me.\nKill them. Kill as many as you can. Bring me their tusks, and we will celebrate their deaths together.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBoar Hunter's Cape Grassland Sash\nExperience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The quilboar will pay for this, ‹name›. I swear it.","done":"‹class›, you take my task seriously, and for that I thank you.\nAlthough my desire for revenge remains, I can at least smile seeing that the quilboars have felt pain themselves.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52,"y":31.6,"n":"Mankrik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96339":{"id":96339,"t":"Legacy reward replica ironforge air rifle","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","rew":"You will receive:\nHolstered Replica Ironforge Air Rifle\nLevel 0 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 96339","cats":["the-barrens"]},"96899":{"id":96899,"t":"Bandarion keep","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Meet Leonid Barthalomew at Bandarion Keep in Tirisfal Glades.","desc":"You've done a great thing for the cause of the Argent Dawn here today, and I thank you. I don't know how familiar you are with the fortress of Bandarion Keep, but my commander and I were headed that way to meet with the paladins that reside there. That was before we learned of the presence of the Cult of the Damned.\nIf you'd like to learn more about the Argent Dawn and our mission, seek out my commander at Bandarion Keep, to the northwest of here. I'll remain here to mop up the rest of this mess.","done":"This place is full of memories for me. This place was once held by the Argent Dawn. It was here from here that we prepared for many battles and skirmishes against the scourge during their most recent push into Tirisfal Glades.\nWhen we withdrew to the Plaguelands I feared it would fall into disrepair. My fear was well-founded, but I am glad that Danitha and her paladins have taken over stewardship of it now.\nShe even named the keep after... a mutual friend.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.8,"y":61,"n":"Hadric Harlson","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.8,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2339":{"id":2339,"t":"Find the Gems and Power Source","lv":44,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover all three gems and a power source for the necklace from Uldaman, and then bring them to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath. Jarkal believes a power source might be found on the strongest construct present in Uldaman.\nFrom the journal, you know...\n* The ruby has been stashed in a barricaded Shadowforge area.\n* The topaz has been hidden in an urn in one of the Trogg areas, near some Alliance dwarves.\n* The sapphire has been claimed by Grimlok, the trogg leader.\nShattered Necklace Ruby Shadowforge Cache\nShattered Necklace Sapphire Grimlok\nShattered Necklace Topaz Conspicuous Urn\nShattered Necklace Power Source Archaedas\nProvided: Bloodstained Journal","desc":"Here is the journal, translated for you to read on your own. The crux of it says dwarves hid the ruby, the troggs hid the topaz, and a trogg named Grimlok has the sapphire.\nLook - you're going to need a power source to make the necklace work again. Dran Droffers doesn't know this. To find one, here's what I'd do: go as deep as you can in Uldaman and kill whatever construct there is the strongest. No doubt whatever that is would have it.\nWhen you have everything collected, come back here!","rew":"Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You've got another trip into the depths of Uldaman in store for yourself if you don't have the gems and a power source capable of channeling magical power back into the necklace.\nYou'll be getting the gems back to deliver to the goons in Orgrimmar; I will be keeping the power source, since it will be the thing that will make the necklace work in the first place...","done":"Very well done, ‹class›. Now the fruits of our redirection will pay themselves out handsomely. I'm finished with the necklace itself, and I am confident I can duplicate the construction process consistently.\nBut first, I will use a specially prepared incantation to quickly analyze those gems before you take them and the necklace back to Orgrimmar. This will take just a brief moment to do.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"1139":{"id":1139,"t":"The Lost Tablets of Will","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Tablet of Will, and return them to Advisor Belgrum in Ironforge.\nTablet of Will Tablet of Will","desc":"We've slowed the Shadowforge clan by cutting them off from Blackrock Spire, but Hammertoe's quest is still unfulfilled. His death must not be in vain. He dreamt of finding the Tablet of Will: a stone shard inscribed with magic by the titans themselves to help imbue their creations with life--making them have a will of their own, or so the legends say.\nWe must still recover the Tablet before the Shadowforge clan finds it.\nReturn to Uldaman, find the tablet, and return here immediately.","rew":"You will receive:\nMedal of Courage\nMoney: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,850\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Hammertoe's quest must be actualized, ‹name›. I owe him that much.\nYour return to Uldaman is imperative not only to that goal, but also to the safety of all dwarven kind. With the tablet in the hands of the Dark Irons who knows how powerful their army of golems would become.","done":"<Advisor Belgrum shakes his head in disbelief as you hand him the stone shard.>\n‹name›, this is amazing. I shall have this brought to the king's mages as soon as possible. They will want to study it to find out if the legends are true. But that is a discussion for another time: you have aided our people more than I would have ever expected--thank you.\nDun Morogh Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":22.6,"n":"Advisor Belgrum","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"4739":{"id":4739,"t":"In Search of Menara Voidrender","lv":31,"min":31,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"‹class›! Yes, you!\nYou don't have all the accoutrements, but it's plain to see you're ready--the air around you exudes greater confidence. Yes, I see it now.\nMenara Voidrender would teach you a few things if you feel you're ready. She spends her time tutoring younger students in the arcane. She even gives gifts to those who pass her tests.\nGo to Ratchet in the Barrens if you're interested. She's above the city in Strahad's tower.","rew":"Experience: 625","done":"Ah, Kaal sent you. Good. Then word does reach far enough to find future students. This pleases me.\nIt is typical of our kind, ‹name›, to band together, regardless of race. It is especially important since those we deal with most do not discriminate in their malice if we fail to appease them or control them properly.\nI feel you've learned a great many things, and if you are willing, I would help you create tools to compliment your skills.\nUndercity The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":86.2,"y":15.9,"n":"Kaal Soulreaper","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8419":{"id":8419,"t":"An Imp's Request","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a piece of felcloth to Impsy in Felwood.\nFelcloth Xorothian Dreadsteed 34.8 % , Felcular 9.9 % , Lord Banehollow 9.9 % , Doomguard Commander 8.6 % and 4 more","desc":"‹name›, an imp in Felwood by the name of Impsy has requested your presence. It is somewhat strange, as he has asked that you bring a piece of felcloth as a sign of good faith. Considering the power you already wield as a warlock, I can only assume you know the satyrs of Felwood carry this felcloth.\nYou can find Impsy just north of the Bloodvenom Falls, which I've heard is quite lovely this time of year.","rew":"Experience: 3,800","back":"Do you have my felcloth?","done":"What a splendid warlock you are!\n<Impsy holds the felcloth to his face.>\nOh how I love the feel of it, the way it burns your skin and weaves evil thoughts through the mind...\nStormwind City Swamp of Sorrows Orgrimmar Undercity Dun Morogh Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85,"n":"Demisette Cloyce","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.9,"y":84.2,"n":"Ursula Deline","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.7,"y":85.7,"n":"Sandahl","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":48.7,"y":55.6,"n":"Kartosh","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48,"y":45.9,"n":"Grol'dar","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.6,"y":47,"n":"Mirket","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Zevrost","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":86.2,"y":15.9,"n":"Kaal Soulreaper","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":86.4,"y":15.3,"n":"Luther Pickman","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":88.9,"y":15.9,"n":"Richard Kerwin","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.3,"y":22.1,"n":"Thistleheart","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.1,"y":22.3,"n":"Alexander Calder","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1699":{"id":1699,"t":"The Rethban Gauntlet","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter the Rethban Caverns, reach the first fork, and return to Yorus Barleybrew within the time allowed.\nYou must not die and release your spirit.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"I call my challenge the Rethban Gauntlet. To pass the trial, all you must do is enter the Rethban Caverns, to the first fork, then return here. Easy! Except there are a few wrinkles...\nYou have to return within an hour.\nThere are whole heaps of Redridge Gnolls in the way.\nBefore you start, you have to take a swig of my family's signature drink: Barleybrew Scalder!\nSo what do you say? The Rethban Caverns are in the foothills north of Lakeshire. Are you ready to run the Rethban Gauntlet?","rew":"Experience: 1,300","back":"Time is wasting, ‹name›. If I were you, I'd get going...","done":"You made it! Well done! Three cheers for ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.5,"y":44.7,"n":"Yorus Barleybrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5059":{"id":5059,"t":"Locked Away","lv":55,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dalson Outhouse Key Wandering Skeleton","back":"The door to the outhouse has begun to splinter at the edges of the frame as though it has been repeatedly and incessantly tried to be forced open. It is currently locked up tight from the outside of the outhouse.\nAs you rattle the door, you hear a guttural moaning come from inside! Whatever is inside there, it certainly does not sound friendly.","done":"Using the key found on the skeleton of the former Mrs. Dalson, you unlock the door to the outhouse. A bloodthirsty ghoul leaps from the outhouse, having been trapped inside for who knows how long.\nIt is clear by the bloodcurdling scream of the ghoul at your presence that the former Farmer Dalson is now beyond saving.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":48.1,"y":49.7,"n":"Outhouse","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5219":{"id":5219,"t":"Target: Dalson's Tears","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Dalson's Tears in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nDalson's Tears Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Malvinious\nEmpty Dalson's Tears Bottle\nProvided: Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle","desc":"One of the plague cauldrons is located in the field of a former farmhouse now referred to as Dalson's Tears. Well, we shall shed no tears this day as we thwart the Scourge and have them choke on their own fumes!\nGo to Dalson's Tears, almost due north of Andorhal, and eliminate the cauldron lord there. It should have a key like the last one did, allowing you into the cauldron. Use this bottle to obtain a sample from inside the cauldron; each cauldron has its own distinct brew of toxins it uses.","rew":"Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"The macabre key found on the cauldron lord easily slides into a keyhole and then disappears, allowing you permanent access to it. Crude, viscous ichors pulsate through twisted tubes within the cauldrons underpinnings.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":46.2,"y":51.9,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92819":{"id":92819,"t":"Destruction in deadmines","lv":18,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the detonator.\nDetonator used","desc":"We are almost finished. Use the detonator, and end this.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"I don't know what to say, Samelyn. To think that Stormwind would put their military ambitions over the livelihood of their people...","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":38.6,"y":83.6,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92579":{"id":92579,"t":"To valanaar","lv":8,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Aonda's Written Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.\nProvided: Aonda's Written Report","desc":"For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to the Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.\nThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.\nAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTraveler's Wraps Adventurer's Cloak Hiking Boots\nExperience: 180\n+10 reputation with Windshapers\n+10 reputation with High Order","back":"A letter from Aonda. What's that crafty highlander been up to?","done":"<Valennia's expression darkens as she reads the letter.>\nAonda trusted you to deliver this and she speaks highly enough of you in this letter, so I'll try to trust you too. Before we speak further, I need to consult with the few peacekeepers we have left here and formulate a plan in case the cult strikes here next. Enjoy your stay in Valanaar for now.\nIf you are looking to keep yourself busy, there are plenty of townsfolk that can likely use the help of a strong young adventurer like yourself.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93459":{"id":93459,"t":"More alaketh ears","lv":13,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Al'Aketh Cultist's Ears from the Al'Aketh in Shadowgale Forest, the Shine of Akir, or Gustberry Lowlands and return them to Vayn Moonclaw in Shadowgale Forest.\n5 Al'Aketh Cultist's Ear","desc":"The Al'Aketh cult normally gives this forest a wide berth, fearing the rumors that it is haunted... rumors we are happy to maintain. The Druids of my order wish only to live quiet, peaceful lives here in Shadowgale and they threaten that.\nMany among us are afraid.\nI come with an offer. Fight the cultists for us, and bring us the ears of those you kill. We will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to our secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.","back":"<Vayn nods at you.>","done":"As promised, here is your reward.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":63.8,"y":36,"n":"Vayn Moongaze","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});